---
import Rescue from '../layouts/Rescue.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
---
<Rescue title="About us" description="About Maple Hollow Animal Rescue." eyebrow="Who we are" heading="About Maple Hollow Animal Rescue" lead="Maple Hollow Animal Rescue is a fictional nonprofit, made up to show Nest Co.'s website and software work. The details here are invented.">
  <div class="wrap body">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="frame"><Photo name="shelter" alt="A staff member kneeling at a kennel door to greet a friendly dog in a bright, clean kennel area." sizes="(min-width: 900px) 45vw, 100vw" /></div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h2>What this site demonstrates</h2>
        <p>The volunteer sign-up and coordinator pages are a small working tool: shifts, spots left, sign-up and cancel, a coverage view and a CSV export. Here the data stays in your browser. For a real organization the same screens would connect to a database or an existing system, with staff logins, email confirmations and reminders.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Rescue>
